# NeMo Gym — code ownership
#
# Encodes the "NeMo Gym Code Component Ownership" map so GitHub auto-requests the
# right reviewers on every PR.
#
# Teams (membership is the source of truth and is maintained by each team's
# maintainers — do not list individuals here):
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_env_benchmarks  Frontier Eval — EM Rita Neves,
#                                    Eng PICs Michal Bien, Marta Stepniewska-Dziubinska
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_core            Core-Arch + RL — EM Bernard Nguyen,
#                                    Eng PIC Ananth Subramaniam
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_architects      Advisors — request for ambiguous, cross-lane,
#                                    or escalated changes; cross-ownership of the repo
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_leads           Leads (EM/PM/TPM) — request mostly for
#                                    documentation, RFCs, and processes
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_maintainers     Maintainers — repository-wide merge authority
#                                    through gym_approvers
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_approvers       Merge approvers — union of Architects, Leads,
#                                    and Gym Maintainers
#   @NVIDIA-NeMo/automation          CI, build, and release infrastructure
#
# The split follows one principle: Core owns the contracts and the substrate,
# Frontier Eval owns the implementations and the evaluation outputs built on top of
# them. So base_responses_api_agent.py (the interface) is Core while every harness
# under responses_api_agents/ is Frontier Eval; rollout_collection.py (the engine) is
# Core while reward_profile.py (what consumes rollouts to make decisions) is
# Frontier Eval.
#
# Two rules this file cannot express, which still apply by policy:
#   1. Breaking changes to shared contracts and user-facing CLI surfaces need
#      sign-off from BOTH lanes, ideally agreed at the proposal stage.
#   2. Well-isolated changes that do not touch core features may be reviewed by
#      other frequent contributors without the code owner.
#
# CODEOWNERS routes component experts for review; these requests are advisory.
# Merge approval is enforced separately by the main-branch ruleset, which requires
# one approval from @NVIDIA-NeMo/gym_approvers. That team is the union of
# Architects, Leads, and Gym Maintainers.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" must remain disabled. Team review
# auto-assignment can turn component-team requests into named reviewers. Every
# CODEOWNERS team below has write access; otherwise GitHub silently ignores it.
#
# Supporting and low-risk paths are intentionally unowned: root tests, docs/,
# fern/, examples/, data/, cache/, results/, scripts/, and top-level files. They
# should not add approval requirements beyond those of the implementation they
# accompany. If one of these paths needs recurring specialist review, add an
# explicit rule rather than a catch-all.

